<title>MACAU: Macau signs air four services agreements.</title>
<headline>Macau signs air four services agreements.</headline>
<dateline>MACAU 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Macau government said on Wednesday it had signed air service agreements with Denmark, Sweden, Norway and North Korea.</p>
<p>The government said Governor Vasco Rocha Vieira signed the agreements with the three Scandinavian nations in Oslo, where he was attending the Nobel Peace Prize award ceremony. It gave no further details.</p>
<p>Scandinavian airline SAS operates regular all-cargo flights to the Portuguese-administered enclave, which borders the southern Chinese province of Guangdong. There are currently no passenger flights between Scandinavia and Macau.</p>
<p>Vieira signed an agreement with North Korea earlier in the month, the government said, adding that North Korean civil aviation officials signed the documents in Macau on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Air Koryo, North Korea's national airline, flies two weekly stopover flights to Macau en route to and from Bangkok.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6441</p>
